course: dictionary
lesson: 9404
title: Spy: three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word spy can be a noun or a verb. A spy is a person who secretly collects information about another country, group or person. To spy on someone is to watch them secretly.
explain: Context tells you which meaning you need. «Spies once used invisible inks, like lemon juice.» Here spies are people who secretly collect information, because they are using secret ink. Swap in your meaning: a person who secretly collects information fits.
explain: «I spy with my little eye, something red» uses spy in a third way. To spy something means to see or notice it. Check it by swapping in see: «I see with my little eye, something red» still makes sense, so this is the right meaning.
fact: Spy means a person who secretly collects information about another country, group or person.
fact: To spy on someone means to watch them secretly, as in «spy on», and the verb forms are spies, spied and spying.
fact: To spy something means to see or notice it, as in «I spy», which is a guessing game where players name things they can see.
fact: «Invisible» means impossible to see, so «lemon-juice writing is invisible» means you cannot read it until the paper is warmed.
fact: Other phrases with spy: «a spy camera» is a small hidden camera, and «spy story» is a story about secret agents.
exercise: Ella says, «I spy with my little eye, something red.» What does spy mean here? | To collect secret information for a country | *To see or notice something | To hide from the police | To fight in a war
exercise: «Spies once used invisible inks, like lemon juice.» What is a spy in this sentence? | *A person who secretly collects information | A fast runner | A kind of pen | A game played in the car
exercise: «Games like I spy, counting number plates and audiobooks make a long car journey pass faster.» Find and copy the word that means quicker. | *faster | counting | journey | audiobooks
test: «To spy on someone» means what? | To give them a present | To run away from them | *To watch them secretly | To shout their name
test: Which sentence uses spy as a verb? | Mia is a spy in the film | *Mia spied on her brother's secret box | The spy story was long | Mia's spy camera was red
exam: Which phrase names a guessing game where players take turns naming things they can see? | *I spy | spy camera | spy on | spy story
